<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Computer History</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #eef6ff;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 15px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #2457a6;
        }

        .year {
            background: #f1f6ff;
            padding: 18px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-left: 5px solid #2457a6;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #2457a6;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>💻 History of Computers</h1>

    <div class="year">
        <h2>1940s — First Computers</h2>
        <p>Early computers were very large machines used mainly for scientific and military calculations.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="year">
        <h2>1950s — Transistors</h2>
        <p>Transistors replaced large vacuum tubes and made computers smaller and more reliable.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="year">
        <h2>1970s — Microprocessors</h2>
        <p>Microprocessors helped make smaller and more affordable computers possible.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="year">
        <h2>1980s — Personal Computers</h2>
        <p>Personal computers became increasingly common in homes, schools and offices.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="year">
        <h2>Today — Modern Computing</h2>
        <p>Computers are now used in education, business, communication, entertainment and science.</p>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
